<title>SWEDEN: Volvo says NedCar to make profit in Nov.</title>
<headline>Volvo says NedCar to make profit in Nov.</headline>
<dateline>GOTHENBURG, Sweden 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish car maker AB Volvo said on Wednesday production at its jointly-owned NedCar plant at Born in the Netherlands would be in the black as early as next month.</p>
<p>&quot;The last car in the 400 series will be produced in mid-November. The 400 series is a loss-making line and that capacity can now be used to manufacture the S40/V40 range,&quot; Volvo spokesman Ingemar Hesslefors told Reuters.</p>
<p>NedCar is owned one-third each by Volvo, Mitsubishi Motors Corp and the Dutch State.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1006</p>
</text>
